Another way of approaching this is to make a distinction between
perception and memory.  Things you can see would show up different
than things you remember seeing.  This could be done with two colors,
two different display attributes, or different symbols entirely.
Making this customizable is probably reasonable.

The next trick is to deal with multiperception: things you can hear,
things you can smell, and so forth.
